SUMMARY
  rank(E_G) <= 0 by all three 2-isogeny Selmer bounds (sharp;
  for theta=-816 equality: im alpha_1 contains {1,2,3,6} = <2,3>,
  dim exactly 2, and <S_B> = {1} forces s_B = 0).
  ALL known points on E_G are torsion: 2*(48,10368) = (Fraction(480, 1), Fraction(0, 1)),
  2*(912,20736) = (Fraction(480, 1), Fraction(0, 1))  -> E_G(Q)_tors = Z/2 x Z/4 (order 8).
  => rank(E_G) = 0.
  => rank J(C3_A) = rank J(C3_B) = rank(E_A) + rank(E_A) + rank(E_G)
                                   = 1 + 1 + 0 = 2 < 3 = genus.
  => Coleman/Chabauty applies IN PRINCIPLE to C3_A and C3_B.
  NAMED GAP: the actual Coleman computation (p-adic annihilation of the
  rank-2 MW basis of J, residue bound  #C(Q) <= #C(F_p) + 2g - 2) has
  NOT been carried out; e.g. p=11 (11 > 2g+1, 11 | disc? no):
  #C3_A(F_11) = 8 would give #C3_A(Q) <= 8 + 4 = 12.
